# blacklist file for block-badips
#
# Each IPv4 or IPv6 address or range which is in a separate line will always be
# blocked by block-badips.sh, even if it is not on the downloaded list, unless
# it is in /etc/block-badips.whitelist.
# Lines containing anything else, like these comments, are ignored.
#
# Examples:
#198.51.100.23
#203.0.113.0/24
#2001:db8::23
#2001:db8:2::/48
